169	\N	253,281,286	9	\N	\N	\N	It is pertinent to mention that Muhammad Arif has been serving as a Research Officer (RO) in the RF Lab, Sensors Division, NRDI since 1 February 2023 and has consistently demonstrated outstanding technical competence, professional growth, and leadership in the field of RF and microwave engineering. Having been associated with NRDI for the past 3 years, he has established himself as a highly capable and dedicated professional. He is a Gold Medalist in Electrical Engineering from PAF-KIET and is currently pursuing his Master’s degree at NUST-PNEC, where he continues to maintain an excellent academic record. Throughout his tenure, he has developed strong expertise in RF design, simulation using industry-standard tools and has made significant contributions to several strategic projects, including the development and enhancement of GNSS Jammer systems, TWT subsystems, and RF Passive Decoy systems. Since March 2026, he has also been leading the RF Group, demonstrating effective leadership, technical excellence, and the ability to successfully manage critical engineering activities. In view of his exceptional technical capabilities, leadership qualities, and consistently high-level performance, he is considered a valuable asset to the organization. It is therefore strongly recommended that he may please be promoted to the position of Senior Research Officer (SRO), along with a revision of his monthly salary from PKR 100,000 to PKR 195,000 in accordance with the new HR policy, in recognition of his valuable contributions and to support the retention of this key resource within the organization.	Furthermore, the contracts of SRO Saad and RO Muhammad Arif expired on 30 June 2026. The cases for the renewal of their contracts, with effect from 1 July 2026, have been submitted for the approval of the DG NRDI. The cases have been proposed for ex post facto approval due to a technical issue that occurred while entering the project details in RDWIS.
170	\N	292	17	\N	\N	\N	It is pertinent to mention that the above-mentioned individual is being hired for the period of 12 months. His salary has been proposed from ECM project for 01 month while salary of remaining 11 months will be proposed from forth coming projects or on-going  projects subject to the availability of funds. His case has been submitted for the approval of MD R&D.	\N
