250003	716	2022-05-21 00:13:58	1.   Competent authority has approved indigenous development of STLT at a cost of Rs 34.68M vide PN/NRD Div/TD DTE/01/2176376 dated 25 Sep 2020.\r\n\r\n2.   Requirement of funds during CFY has been forwarded to NHQ vide PI letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/6894086 dated 09 Oct 2020.  Amount of Rs 12.5 Million has been approved for 2020-2021 as per the verbal information shared by concerned authority.  However, request for enhancement/ revision of funds to cater for MTSS/ PNBA / Bahria Foundation share has also been forwarded to NHQ. PI letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/8641220 dated 11 March 2021 refers. \r\n\r\n3.   Project team visited the submarine installed at Pakistan Maritime museum on 19 Jan 2021, for awareness and understanding of Submarine assembly and its functionality. Team also visited STC and Navigation School on 21 Jan 2021 and observed various simulators installed at STC/ Navigation School. \r\n\r\n4.   Meeting of Director ET with MTSS team was held to brief them about the scope and modalities of the project. Subsequently, MTSS HQ, after due process at its end, forwarded the work order to NHQ for further necessary action.\r\n\r\n5.   T0 yet to be established. Work order is under process at NHQ.  Development work will be initiated upon availability of allocated funds.\r\n\r\n6.   Meeting chaired by VCNS was held on 14 Sep 21 and subsequently Minutes of Meeting have been received vide reference PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 2021.\r\n\r\n7.     As per Para 12-C of MoM of above mentioned meeting, Development of STLT may be considered after development of Virtual Reality (VR) Center.\r\n\r\n8.     RDW has initiated a letter w.r.t processing of VRC and STLT cases separately. RDW letter PN/DG NRDI/R AND D Wing/03/11015633 dated 27 Oct 21 is relevant in this regard. Salient of the letter are provided below:\r\na.   VR based STLT is an ops requirement raised by STC and supported by COMPAK Command being the end user. \r\nb.   Current basic VR facility at R&D Wing (i.e an extension of VA Lab at PG Block of PNS JAUHAR) is ready to develop STLT simulator. Therefore, STLT and VRC may be processed as separate projects, independent of each other. \r\nc.   Budgetary proposal of VRC mainly includes hardware infrastructure. Whereas, VR based projects like STLT mostly covers processing and delivery equipment along-with HR requirement with an aim to enhance capacity and capability. \r\nd.   DSMO, being Sponsoring Dte, may be approached for processing and issuance of STLT Work Order as per procedure in vogue. \r\ne.   In parallel, relevant sponsoring directorate may be approached for processing of funds and work order issuance for VRC Project.  In this regard, draft PPF and URD have also been shared with Dir R&D.\r\n9.    STLT PPF and URD was forwarded to NHQ by Dir STC through COMKAR for processing as per NRDI Directive. The same has been received duly recommended by DCNS(O) vide Dir R&D letter PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3364653 dated 3 Dec 21.\r\n\r\n10.    STLT PPF and URD, as received from NHQ alongwith VR based STLT project proposal (prepared by ET Div) duly recommended by DG NRDI, has been forwarded to ACNS (NRD) at NHQ on 7 Dec 21 for further processing. RDW Letter PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11643713 dated 7 Dec 21 refers in this regard.\r\n\r\n11.   Initial PoC of STLT has been developed. Demonstration of same was presented to CNS on his visit to NRDI on 8 Dec 21 in ET Div VR Lab.	DEnab	Finalized	2022-06-03 02:29:45	25	Apr 22	-19-25-	-19-25-19-	f	\N
