350002	217	2020-10-07 12:10:59	\r\n1.   GPS Spoofing.\r\n\r\na.   Hardware Assembly. Ruggedized housing and assembly of spoofing PoC equipment is completed.\r\n\r\n\r\nb.   Development of End user GUI. GUI has been successfully developed. Alpha testing for the software is under progress.\r\n\r\nc.   Acceptance Trials. Prepared Trial Sheets have been approved by Naval Headquarter NHQ vide letter PN/NCW/03/2500137 dated 22 Sep 20. The trials are planned at GHARO site in week commencing 26th Oct 20.\r\n\r\nd.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR).\r\n\r\n2.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container is in progress. The INTELL team visited the M/s RIMS facility and finalized the contours of equipment installation. The said activity will be completed by Oct 20.\r\n3.   Miscellaneous Studies Supporting PN Fleet and Repair Agencies undertaken during reporting period\r\n\r\na.   First set of training modules of PA UT (Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing) equipment Omni Scan MX2 for Dockyard Lab staff is completed. Dockyard staff is also attached for OJT.\r\n\r\nb.   Ultrasonic Testing (UT) of Besconds used in the cable hull passage onboard S/Ms. UT of a neoprene based locally developed besconds was undertaken. The bescond is rejected due presence of flaws / voids at multiple locations.\r\n\r\nc.   500W High Power Antenna for PAF\r\n\r\n1)   INTELL NRDI received a URD from PAF 606 Workshop, as approved by competent authority at NHQ, for development of a high power jamming Log Periodic Dipole Array Antenna capable of working at RF power of 300W.\r\n\r\n2)   A preliminary electromagnetic design was developed by RF team which satisfied following requirements of the URD:\r\n\r\na)   Bandwidth: 1-3 GHz\r\nb)   Gain 8 dBi\r\nc)   Power Rating >300W\r\n\r\n3)   Thermal analysis of the high power antenna was also carried out in ANSYS Fluent, and results revealed safe operation at 500W.\r\n\r\n4)   The antenna is currently being fabricated.	DSensors	Edited	2020-10-12 11:34:25	38	Sep 20	-20-25-30-38-	\N	f	\N
