er. \r\nb.   Current basic VR facility at R&D Wing (i.e an extension of VA Lab at PG Block of PNS JAUHAR) is ready to develop STLT simulator. Therefore, STLT and VRC may be processed as separate projects, independent of each other. \r\nc.   Budgetary proposal of VRC mainly includes hardware infrastructure. Whereas, VR based projects like STLT mostly covers processing and delivery equipment along-with HR requirement with an aim to enhance capacity and capability. \r\nd.   DSMO, being Sponsoring Dte, may be approached for processing and issuance of STLT Work Order as per procedure in vogue. \r\ne.   In parallel, relevant sponsoring directorate may be approached for processing of funds and work order issuance for VRC Project.  In this regard, draft PPF and URD have also been shared with Dir R&D.\r\n\r\n9.    STLT PPF and URD was forwarded to NHQ by Dir STC through COMKAR for processing as per NRDI Directive. The same has been received duly recommended by DCNS(O) vide Dir R&D letter PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3364653 dated 3 Dec 21.\r\n\r\n10.    STLT PPF and URD, as received from NHQ alongwith VR based STLT project proposal (prepared by ET Div) duly recommended by DG NRDI, has been forwarded to ACNS (NRD) at NHQ on 7 Dec 21 for further processing. RDW Letter PN/DG NRDI/At PNS JAUHAR/03/11643713 dated 7 Dec 21 refers in this regard.\r\n\r\n11.   Initial PoC of STLT has been developed. Demonstration of same was presented to CNS on his visit to NRDI on 8 Dec 21 in ET Div VR Lab.	DEnab	Finalized	2022-08-02 23:14:49	25	May 22	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
