350012	579	2021-12-02 18:58:47	1.   Workorder Issuance. The T0 is established as 10 Jun 21 vide letter ILS/0620/INVENTORY MODEL dated 03 Aug 21. Formulation of the acceptance committee as per the requirement of work order is in progress. \r\n\r\n2.   Finalized Case Study. A detailed study of Machining Control System (MCS) of YARMOOK class ship and SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. The case study was reviewed by NCMA and INTELL NRDI team incorporated the recommendations. Finalized Case Study report submitted Oct against Milestone-3 for release of funds has been evaluated and supported vide PN/NCMA/03/10738145 dated 06 Oct 21. \r\n\r\n\r\n3.   SR-60 RADAR. A detailed study on SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. Technical documentation and defect history of the RADAR has been received. A visit was carried out by the project team to identify potential data acquisition points for periodic NDT data collection and shortlist data-loggers deployment locations inside the RADAR cabinet. The team visited SR-60 RADAR onboard PNS ASLAT on 29th October 2021 to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of a functional RADAR system. The team performed thermal, magnetic and ultrasonic non-destructive testing at accessible data acquisition points. The shortlisted data acquisition points and NDT data collection methodology was also briefed to the accompanied FMG staff. The recorded NDT data is maintained in a historical database for analytics.\r\n\r\n4.   Procurement and development of Dataloggers. Magnetic flux leakage and environmental monitoring sensors have been procured and are being tested. Printed circuit board (PCB) based data-loggers are being developed for recording equipment environmental conditions and magnetic non-destructive testing (NDT) data. The developed dataloggers will subsequently be installed on SR-60 RADAR and MCS onboard PN Ship.\r\n\r\n5.   Survey Visit. INTELL NRDI team embarked PNS TABUK for sea trip to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of onboard Machinery Control System (MCS). Thermal and ultrasonic emission data of different MCS sensors installed on running engines (ME-1 & ME-4) as well as the ambient signals were recorded. The acquired data will be analyzed to identify potential data acquisition points that embed health information of the MCS. The list of MCS sensors used for data acquisition for each running engine is provided below. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\na.   Main Engine Exhaust Temperature Sensor\r\nb.   Main Engine Jacket Water Temperature Sensor\r\nc.   Main Engine Oil-Mist Detection Sensor\r\nd.   Main Engine PORT-side Cylinders 1-8\r\ne.   Main Engine STBD-side Cylinders 1-8\r\nf.   Main Engine Turbo Chargers 1- 2\r\ng.   I/O Module 1\r\nh.   I/O Module 2\r\nj.         Display Module 1\r\nk.        Display Module 2	DSensors	Cancelled	2021-12-03 09:12:30	20	Nov 21	-20-	\N	f	\N
