350013	640	2022-01-02 15:49:13	\r\n1.   VTS qualification in vicinity of ESM Detectors onboard PN ATR. M/s RAS highlighted that the high-power density and E-Field of LoS VTS transmission will affect the performance of onboard ESM system. It is recommended that both systems should not be operated simultaneously to ensure smooth operation. The same recommendation has been forwarded to NHQ vide letter PN/DGNRDI/RANDDWING/03110878134 dated 15 Oct 21. \r\n\r\n2.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI. The civil work required for installation of GT&RS at RDS NATHIAGALI is being undertaken by M/s FAST team. Tower construction for radome base has been completed. The radome is also mounted on the tower. GT&RS equipment installation is in progress by NRDI INTELL in collaboration with M/s FAST. Integration of Directional Antenna Director (DAD) system in radome and testing will be completed by mid Jan 22.\r\n\r\n3.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at RDS MIANWALI. Site proposed by NRDI INTELL at RDS MIANWALI for installation of Antenna Radome was not recommended by HQ COMCOAST, being close to the edge of the cliff vide letter PN / HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. HQ COMCOAST suggested 02 x alternate sites near Defcom building for the installation of said system. However, the alternate sites proposed by the HQ COMCOAST are not considered feasible as receiving system will be subjected to blanking due to higher terrain on seaward side. HQ COMCOAST has been requested to review the site proposed by NRDI vide PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21.\r\n\r\n4.   Installation of Radome/ Steel Structure for GT&RS at GWADAR. All construction works at GWADAR Hammerhead have been halted due to some cracks being observed, as informed vide letter PN / HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. NRDI INTELL has requested HQ COMCOAST to share the report pertaining to Geo Hazard study of the area, if available, 