/ HQ COASTAL COMMAND /03/11311292 dated 16 Nov 21. NRDI INTELL has requested HQ COMCOAST to share the report pertaining to Geo Hazard study of the area, if available, to evaluate the alternate suitable location vide reference PN/ DG NRDI/R AND D WING/03/11409842 dated 30 Nov 21.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-31 09:57:11	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350012	591	2021-12-03 09:12:42	\r\n1.   Work Order Issuance. The T0 is established as 10 Jun 21 vide letter ILS/0620/INVENTORY MODEL dated 03 Aug 21. Formulation of the acceptance committee as per the requirement of work order is in progress. \r\n\r\n2.   Finalized Case Study. A detailed case study of Machining Control System (MCS) of YARMOOK class ship and SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. The case study was reviewed by NCMA and INTELL NRDI team incorporated the recommendations. Finalized Case Study report submitted against Milestone-3 for release of funds has been evaluated and supported vide PN/NCMA/03/10738145 dated 06 Oct 21. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   SR-60 RADAR. A detailed study on SR-60 RADAR has been carried out. Technical documentation and defect history of the RADAR has been received. A visit was carried out by the project team to identify potential data acquisition points for periodic NDT data collection and shortlist data-loggers deployment locations inside the RADAR cabinet. The team visited SR-60 RADAR onboard PNS ASLAT on 29th October 2021 to analyze actual operational and environmental conditions of a functional RADAR system. The team performed thermal, magnetic and ultrasonic non-destructive testing at accessible data acquisition points. The shortlisted data acquisition points and NDT data collection methodology was also briefed to the accompanied FMG staff. The recorded NDT data is maintained in a historical database for analytics. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n4.   Deployment of Dataloggers. Magnetic flux leakage and environmental monitoring sensors have been developed and tested for recording environmental and magnetic data. The developed dataloggers have been installed on SR-60 RADAR and MCS onboard PN Ships. \r\n\r\n5.   Historical Database Development. A historical database is being developed to record the thermal and ultrasonic NDT data acquired from NRDI INTELL identified test points onboard PN ships. The acquired NDT is being analyzed at NRDI INTELL. The environmental data acquired form dataloggers will also be incorporated in the historical database. Subsequently, data analytics will be performed on the developed database.	DSensors	Finalized	2021-12-31 10:00:55	25	Nov 21	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
