350004	666	2022-03-03 15:09:09	\r\n1.   Change in The Scope of Project. The project scope has been revised in VCNS IHD meeting, vide reference PN/ NDR DIV/ R AND D DTE/03/3240447 dated 05 Oct 21. Operating range of UCAV is limited to 200 km and BLOS operation requirements are eliminated. In this regard, SATCOM and EOIR systems are also removed from the scope. The timeline is also revised to 18 months. Following documents have been submitted in lines with the requirement of IHD meeting:\r\n\r\na.   Revised timeline and itemized cost were forwarded vide letter PN/DG NRDI/ R AND D Wing/03/11125889 dated 02 Nov 21.\r\n\r\nb.   Itemized cost estimates for procurement plan and pertinent details related to procurement source was forwarded vide reference PN/DG NRDI/ At PNS JAUHAR/03/11526644 dated 29 Nov 21. \r\n\r\nc.   Combined draft work order amounting to PKR 238M and corresponding technical and budgetary proposal were forwarded vide letter PN/DG NRDI/At JAUHAR/03/11715770 dated 10 Dec 21.\r\n\r\n2.   Phase-II Work Order. Work order for phase 2 is still awaited. Case for CFA approval is under progress at NHQ. Dir R&D requested to forward list of hardware for hardware milestones and technical proposal for further processing of case, vide reference PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3563370 dated 1 Mar 22. Letter add\r\n\r\n3.   Critical Design of UCAV. Study on selection of actuators for control surfaces and landing gear underway. Electrohydraulic servo valve systems are being considered to implement a fully redundant control system for control surfaces. Upon conclusion of study, quotations will be requested from vendors for relevant components/systems. Design for integration of fuel circuit and engine into airframe is underway. Design of linkage for retraction mechanism of landing gear is also in progress. Actuators for control surfaces and landing gear will be selected after design studies are completed. \r\n\r\n4.   Test Bench for ROTAX Engine. Construction of test bench along with integration of mechanical and electrical components has been completed. Custom designed instrument panel for monitoring engine parameters during testing has also been completed. A gascolator which is required for the fuel circuit in order to filter the fuel before reaching the engine has also been procured. Design of Bowden cable and throttle control mechanism has also been completed and manufacturing of components will be initialized in Jan ’22. Final QC and safety checks will be carried out once manufactured parts will be received. \r\n\r\n5.   Machine Shop. Hartford CNC has been received at serial production facility and placed in the designated area.  Commissioning of the CNC is in progress and will be completed in early Feb ’22. Requirements for air compressor have been finalized. An external enclosed area will be designated outside machine shop for the compressor. On-site survey of the air compressor enclosure has been carried out and construction work has been started. A curing oven for the manufacturing of large parts has been designed in-house. Design specifications have been forwarded to vendor and item has been designed. Initial QC will be carried out once oven is ready.\r\n\r\n6.   Team development. In-house interviews for hardware design engineers have been conducted and suitable candidates for hiring have been shortlisted. \r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2022-03-30 08:53:37	25	Feb 22	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
