350009	245	2020-11-09 14:56:53	1.   Ruggedized UAV Jammer (Eagle Hunt-01).  \r\n\r\n   a.   1st Batch Deployment. EH-01 batch-I is successfully deployed and tested at following sites vide letter PN/NCW/03/2496144 dated 18 Sept 20.\r\n\r\n      (1)   GKA- Greater KARSAZ Area (4th FP) on 28 Sep 20 – 3 Oct 20\r\n      (2)   PN Dockyard (2nd FP) on 5 - 11 Oct 20\r\n      (3)   NRC, ISB (1st FP) on 12 – 18 Oct 20\r\n\r\n   b.   During the deployment following activities were performed by INTELL Team:\r\n\r\n      (1)   Presentations/ Tutorials. Presentations were given to Marines covering all the details related to EH-01 system, its functionality, operating instructions and maintenance instructions for better operational understanding of the complete EH-01 system. \r\n\r\n      (2)   Handing over of Documentation. All necessary jammer documents (Technical manual and Operator manuals) were handed over to the teams. The documents include all aspects of operation, troubleshooting, maintenance and software details.\r\n\r\n      (3)   Training. EH-01 ruggedized jammer handling, operation and safety training were provided to Marines. \r\n\r\n      (4)   Trials. Jamming trials were also conducted in presence of Marines for the Proof of Concept and better understanding of system operation.\r\n\r\n      (5)   Exam. An exam was conducted by the INTELL team for assessing the understanding of Marines on EH-01 system operation. \r\n\r\n3.   2nd Batch Procurement. International procurement for 2nd batch has been initiated. Orders are placed for the hardware equipment; expected delivery is by end Nov 20. Local procurement is also in process.\r\n\r\n4.   Serial Production Facility (SPF). Construction of Layup facility/ paint shop (shed and floor) is completed	DSensors	Finalized	2020-11-11 10:33:45	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	\N	f	\N
350003	262	2020-11-11 10:30:29	1.   Lab Development has been completed with installation of ESD mats, earthing point and power sockets. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n2.   Magnetron Injection Locking Simulation. Modelling and simulation studies indicate requirements of control loops, to enable frequency-injection and phase locking of free running magnetrons for bandwidth reduction for efficient power combining. Work is in progress to design and implement the control loops.\r\n\r\nPoint recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n3.   Control System Designing for Frequency Pushing.\r\n\r\n      a.   Multiple simulation studies have been undertaken on MATLAB© Simulink to model frequency pushing of a Voltage Controlled Oscillator (VCO), using Phase Locked Loop (PLL) techniques. The VCO was successfully locked at a fixed frequency.\r\n\r\n      b.   Simulations are currently being undertaken on PSpice© to develop control circuitry, which will be implemented experimentally on a VCO.\r\n\r\n4.   RF Devices. Waveguide circulators equipped with biased ferrite disks, and waveguide directional couplers, are required in project experimentation. As limited funds have been released, inhouse design and development of RF devices is in progress.\r\n\r\n        a.   The fabrication of waveguide circulator and directional coupler has been started. \r\n\r\n      b.   A constant current power supply required for biasing the electromagnets and tuning the circulator response, is also being designed.\r\n\r\n5.   RF Power Amplifier. In-house design and optimization of 100W power amplifier has been completed. \r\n\r\n6.   Hardware Procurement.  Procurement of coaxial circulators, coaxial terminations, waveguide transitions, waveguide terminations, waveguide adapters, programmable switch mode power supplies and FPGA boards is in process. Phase Locked Loop (PLL) frequency synthesizer ICs and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) ICs are also being procured.\r\n\r\n7.   Feasibility study on in-house development of anechoic chamber is completed.	DR&D	Finalized	2020-11-11 10:31:00	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
350002	261	2020-11-11 10:27:39	1.   GPS Spoofing Hardware Development.\r\n\r\n      a.   Hardware Assembly. Ruggedized housing and assembly of spoofing PoC equipment is completed. Point recommended to be dropped.\r\n\r\n      b.   Development of End user GUI. The GUI has been updated to make it more user friendly. Alpha testing on the software is complete and associated recommendations have been implemented.  Beta testing is under progress and will be completed in first week of Nov 20.\r\n\r\n      c.   Laboratory Trials. with ruggedized housing and spoofing PoC assembly have been concluded SAT.\r\n\r\n      d.   Technical and operator manuals are in the review phase.\r\n\r\n      e.   Acceptance Trials are planned in 2nd week of Nov 20.\r\n\r\n2.   Force Majeure has been invoked by DITD due COVID pandemic. The delivery of 3D X-Band RADAR is also delayed due to export permit processing delays caused by COVID 19 pandemic. Once 3D X-band RADAR will be received, 8-10 weeks are required for customization and testing of Eagle Hunt -3C version (autonomous GPS spoofing using X-band RADAR).\r\n\r\n3.   Housing of reactive jamming equipment in the marinized container through M/s RIMS facility will be completed by Nov 20.	DR&D	Finalized	2020-11-11 10:29:34	25	Oct 20	-20-25-	-20-25-	f	\N
