350006	871	2023-02-03 06:16:29	1.   Aerial Testing of MARLIN-01 UAV. MARLIN-01 UAV platform is prepared for flight testing/ launch trials and available for GBAD firing vide letter PN/NRDI/R AND D WING/03/3718153 dated 01 Aug 22. Subsequently, Post-flight data analysis will be undertaken for further consolidation of the platform. Test flying of (HSTD) was successfully conducted at UAV site BIN QASIM vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/2380342 dated 10 Jan 23. Developed HSTD successfully achieved flight speed upto ~150 knots and gained altitude of ~590 ft. \r\n\r\n2.   Ground Testing of MARLIN-02 UAV. ATPs with relevant international standards duly qualifying the acceptance procedure for similar type of UAVs have already been forwarded to NHQ for perusal vide reference letter no. PN/HQ NRDI/R AND D WING/03/13317845 dated 21 May 22. Ground trials are successfully conducted on 20 Oct 22. Subsequently, aerial testing will be carried out.\r\n\r\n3.   Issuance of PRO against Completed Milestones. Cases of issuance of PROs against already completed milestones, MS 4&5, were submitted vide references MTSS/20/NRDI/HSTD-II/176 dated 20 Jun 22 and MTSS/20/NRDI/HSTD-II/612 dated 31 Oct 22. However, the same has been returned by NHQ vide letter NRD/0404/HSTD/Phase II/546 dated 30 Nov 22 while linking the issuance of PROs with the completion of milestone MS-6. However, payments as per milestones are well defined in the issued Work Order. As MS 4&5 have already been completed, hence, linking issuance of PROs for completed milestones is not as per the issued Work Order. This is affecting the project progress with procurement cases of over PKR 1M are help up for payments to vendors.   Priority issuance of PROs against already completed milestones and subsequent release of payment is required to enable work completion leading to the accomplishment of milestone MS-6. The same has been requested to NHQ vide MTSS letter MTSS/20/NRDI/HSTD-II/365 dated 12 Dec 22.	DSensors	Finalized	2023-02-08 12:02:17	25	Jan 23	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
