350020	1230	2024-04-09 09:41:05.71	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Hardware Lab Assembly. Team visited GHARO on 9 Jan 24 for ground testing of LUNA RF and Avionics components. RF testing of Primary and secondary datalink antennas on GCS along with Remaining GCS side RF components such as attenuator, RF cables and BMR 120 has also been completed along with relevant ATP and ATR. Hardware lab assembly report is submitted. \r\n\r\n2.   Lab & Field Trials. Lab and field trials of the system were successfully carried out.\r\n\r\n3.   Training of AED Personnel. Training plan has been formulated and shared with AED, vide reference. In this regard, AED has nominated reps to attend the said training sessions, vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/7970758 Dated 29 Mar 24.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:25:07.082	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350025	1228	2024-04-09 09:38:48.394	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   CDR Submission. The "Critical Design Report" (CDR) has been submitted against Milestone M6. \r\n\r\n2.   Procurement. Sintering furnace is being procured which will be utilized for development of cathode.\r\n\r\n3.   Design Activities. Reverse engineering for dimensional analysis and material characterization using XRF analyzer held with NRDI is in progress. Moreover, heater design, Electron Gun and slow wave structure designing is in progress. Power supply of existing TWT of LR66 radar is received at NRDI INTELL which will be utilized in this project. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of Waveguide to Coaxial Adapter for cold testing of existing TWT on VNA.\r\n\r\n       b.   Heater Design: Sample heater coil has been successfully designed and manufactured. The manufacturing process has been established. The final design of heater coil will be developed based on calculation of cathode temperature and work function. \r\n\r\n       c.   Pierce Electron Gun: Simulation of Pierce electron Gun is also been revised after finalization of SWS.\r\n\r\n       d.   Slow Wave Structure: Design has been completed. \r\n\r\n       e.   Collector Design:  Collector is being redesigned in accordance with beam spent curve analysis of slow wave structure. \r\n\r\n4.   Development of ARRC. Advance radar research center (ARRC) is being developed at manufacturing facility PNS KARSAZ. Design of ARRC has been completed whereas, development of Clean room is in progress. Procurement of Molecular Vacuum Pump & Bio Safety Cabinet is in progress.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:24:16.343	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350024	1234	2024-04-09 09:46:14.319	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Submission of Project Plan and List of Deliverables. The "Project Plan and List of Deliverables" has been submitted against Milestone M2. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   Submission of Design Report & Drawings. Design of Radome assembly has been completed. Structural analysis for verification of design is also completed. A report encompassing the design details is submitted, against Milestone M4. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission. \r\n\r\n3.   Manufacturing of Radome and Base. Manufacturing of these parts in line with already developed detailed drawings has been completed. The developed parts have been sent to PND for acceptance testing, against Milestone M6. Through pressure testing, the structural integrity of Radome has been qualified. The initial design of Radome also successfully resisted water ingress up-to 44 bar pressure. However, water ingress is observed at 45 bar pressure. Design upgradations have been made in the material of Radome base, its thread size, location and size of seal groove. After design updates, the Radome has successfully passed ingress protection at 45 bar pressure.\r\n\r\n4.   Handover and Testing. The pressure (45 bar for 1 hour) and RF testing is successfully conducted. The developed Radome has been handed over to PND for acceptance.\r\n\r\n5.   Alternative flange design. A design modification of flange is being carried out to improve sealing performance and ease of installation. In this approach the flange will be tightened by means of bolts of known strength and tightening torques.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:21:43.514	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350022	1235	2024-04-09 09:46:59.614	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Antenna Design. Dish antenna has been designed and developed at NRDI INTELL. Patch feeder is also developed.    \r\n\r\n2.   Final Testing & Field Trials of 1st Prototype. FATs and aerial trials were successfully conducted with 01 x NRDI developed dish antenna and were found satisfactory with a range of 54 NM vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1038701 dated 01 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n3.   Delivery of 03 DA. 03 x Dish Antennas with all associated accessories handed over to rep of 47 Sqn vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1326593 dated 18 Sep 23. Successful HATs and aerial trials of 03 x Dish Antenna have also been conducted.\r\n\r\n4.   Delivery of Support Structure. 03 x Support structure for BSE Dish were handed over to 47 Sqn vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1419950 dated 11 Oct 23.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-05-02 12:23:14.775	25	Mar 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350004	1276	2024-07-08 15:18:46.816	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Phase-II Work Order. The work order for phase 2 is still awaited. The earliest issuance of WO is requested in order to retain the trained project HR. \r\n\r\n2.   Space Requirement for UCAV Development. Allocation of PNS BAHADUR drill shed for shifting of NRDI M/SPF to undertake UCAV development is awaited. NHQ letter PN/NRD DIV/R AND D DTE/03/3754293 dated 02 Jun 22 refers.\r\n\r\n3.   For earlier issuance of the WO case has been processed with NHQ vide letter PN/NDRI/GENERAL/4586185 dated 01 Jun 23.\r\n\r\n4.   NRDI has successfully developed test bench for the ROTAX engine, the test bench is fully operational and capable of monitoring multiple parameters. Moreover, during the COMPAK Command presentation held on 26 Apr 22, perused by the Chief of the Naval Staff vide reference PN/NO Dte/OPERATIONS /1101791 dated 03 Jul 23, it has been decided that the NRDI is to be engaged to establish I&D level maintenance setup / limited R&D of CH4. PPF and URD have been received. Work on technical and budgetary proposal will be started upon identification of airworthiness certification body from NHQ.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-08-01 14:57:47.297	25	Jun 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350028	1239	2024-05-14 09:51:16.77	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Project Plan Submission. The "Global Project Plan" (GPP) has been submitted against Milestone M2. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n2.   HPO Submission. The "Hardware Purchase Order" (HPO) has been submitted against Milestone M3. The same has been forwarded to MTSS for invoice and onward submission.\r\n\r\n3.   Detailed Design Report. Milestone M4 (Submission of Detailed Design Report) has been submitted.\r\n\r\n4.   Sourcing of Heat Sink. Required 5 kW Heat Sink was received and tested with 02 kW magnetron. Same heat sink will be utilized as load for effective power combination of 4 x S band 1KW magnetrons.\r\n\r\n5.   Study for Next Phase. Study for development of high power electromagnetic sources for enhance lethality and extended ranges is in progress.\r\n\r\n6.   Design Activities. \r\n\r\n       a.   Design of antenna mode converter for enhanced gain from TE10 to TE11 is completed along with conical antenna. Fabrication of mode converter is complete. \r\n\r\n7.   Lab Testing. Lab testing with 04 x Magnetrons is completed. \r\n\r\n8.   Field Testing. Manufacturing of 01x Conical Horn antenna is completed. Field testing will be performed shortly.	DSensors	Draft	\N	19	Apr 24	-19-	\N	t	\N
