350012	1260	2024-07-08 15:02:10.724	Progress \r\n\r\n1.   Training of Personnel: 14 x Personnel (from NCMA, FMG (WE), FMG (ME), RD & TA, W&S, S & S, SW and ITRF) were earmarked and trained for Operation/ Installation and Maintenance, from 04 Sep 23 to 15 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n2.   GUI Development. The Graphical User Interface (GUI) pertaining to the developed framework has been updated based on the received feedback during training and vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. \r\n\r\n3.   Documentation. The documentation of the project has been updated based on the received feedback vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/1036919 dated 31 Aug 23. The documentation of the project has been forwarded to MTSS as well as NCMA vide PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1320116 dated 28 Sep 23. The document (4-NRDI-RULMANUAL-08100-001-000-0) saliently covers theoretical concepts, Operation of the RUL framework, data acquisition, uploading, diagnosis, prognosis and RUL estimation.  \r\n\r\n4.   Acceptance. ATPs were conducted on 07 Dec 23, subsequently feedback/observations were received from NCMA against conducted ATPs vide letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/6499087 dated 13 Dec 23. In response NRDI wrote a detailed response of received observation vide letter PN/ R AND D WING/PROJECTS/6595648 dated 19 Dec 23. A meeting was held on 11 Jan 24 between NCMA, FMG and NRDI for clarification of response sent by NRDI. Moreover, acceptance from NCMA has been received vide PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/7020919 dated 31 Jan 24 and is under process at NHQs. Hardware (2 x PCs, 6 x Data loggers, 01 x DVD) against Milestone-9 also ready for delivery. However, NCMA has requested to hold hardware provision till acceptance of the Milestone-6 by NHQs. NCMA letter PN/NCMA/PROJECTS/7627804 dated 29 Feb 2024 and NRDI letter PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/7546684 dated 24 Feb 24 refers. NHQ is further approached vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/9080650 dated 26 June 24 for earlier acceptance and inclusion in MMS of the critical/earmarked items.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-08-01 14:57:25.509	25	Jun 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350020	1263	2024-07-08 15:06:32.403	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Hardware Lab Assembly. Team visited GHARO on 9 Jan 24 for ground testing of LUNA RF and Avionics components. RF testing of Primary and secondary datalink antennas on GCS along with Remaining GCS side RF components such as attenuator, RF cables and BMR 120 has also been completed along with relevant ATP and ATR. Hardware lab assembly report is submitted. \r\n\r\n2.   Lab & Field Trials. Lab and field trials of the system were successfully carried out.\r\n\r\n3.   Training of AED Personnel. Training plan has been formulated and shared with AED, vide reference. In this regard, AED has nominated reps to attend the said training sessions, vide reference PN/COMNAV/MAINTENANCE/7970758 Dated 29 Mar 24. Training started on 02 May 24. 02x weeks training completed, however, GCS components training is pending due unavailability of GCS from AED. HQ COMPAK informed same vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/MAINTENANCE/9161338 dated 01 Jul 24.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-08-01 14:58:23.556	25	Jun 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350022	1265	2024-07-08 15:07:58.592	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Antenna Design. Dish antenna has been designed and developed at NRDI INTELL. Patch feeder is also developed.    \r\n\r\n2.   Final Testing & Field Trials of 1st Prototype. FATs and aerial trials were successfully conducted with 01 x NRDI developed dish antenna and were found satisfactory with a range of 54 NM vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1038701 dated 01 Sep 23.\r\n\r\n3.   Delivery of 03 DA. 03 x Dish Antennas with all associated accessories handed over to rep of 47 Sqn vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/PROJECTS/1326593 dated 18 Sep 23. Successful HATs and aerial trials of 03 x Dish Antenna have also been conducted.\r\n\r\n4.   Delivery of Support Structure. 03 x Support structure for BSE Dish were handed over to 47 Sqn vide reference PN/R AND D WING/GENERAL/1419950 dated 11 Oct 23.	DSensors	Finalized	2024-08-01 14:57:54.23	25	Jun 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
350026	1267	2024-07-08 15:09:15.929	Progress\r\n\r\n1.   Milestones Completion.\r\n\r\n       a.   MS4 of the project “Critical Design Report (CDR)” has been completed and submitted on 07 Jul 23.\r\n\r\n       b.   MS5 of the project “Hardware Purchase Order (HPO)” has been completed and submitted on 18 Jul 23.\r\n\r\n       c.   MS6 of the project “Installation of Filter onboard MCMV” is completed.\r\n\r\n       d.   MS7 of the project “Final Testing and Field Trials of PoC 1” is completed and is submitted for acceptance.\r\n\r\n2.   Trials of Sine Wave Filter. \r\n\r\n       a.   Installation of OEM recommended Sine Wave filter onboard PNS MUJAHID in ungrounded configuration to accrue optimum performance was undertaken by NRDI INTELL. Subsequently, check raging was conducted on 15 Mar 24 at ORMARA by MTC with NRDI reps in presence to ascertain filter efficacy.\r\n\r\n       b.   Report reveals maximum reduction of 27 dB at port side and 11.6 dB at Stbd side APM with application of filter, vide reference PN/R AND D WING/8362390 dated 30 Apr 24.\r\n\r\n       c.   In view of trials performed, signed Milestone 07 (Final Testing and Field Trials PoC -01) is received vide reference PN/HQ COMPAK/MAINTENANCE/9138757 dated 04 Jul 24.  \r\n\r\n3.   Development of SFC based solution.\r\n\r\n       a.   SFC based APM drive system of  Ex-ALKAMAR class ship is being undertaken at NRDI INTELL vide reference, PN/M AND HE WING/GENERAL/1984727 dated 28 Mar 24. \r\n\r\n       b.   Thyristor Based (inverter + chopper configuration) solution is required for said application as such inverters are more effective low frequency motors such as APMs.\r\n\r\n       c.   Different OEM are being approached to acquire desired solution. Upon finalization of any viable option, proposal will be submitted.  \r\n\r\n?	DSensors	Finalized	2024-08-01 14:57:02.155	25	Jun 24	-19-25-	\N	f	\N
